$ diff -u docs/blog-ops/house-upgrade-stardew/lock/en/body.md docs/blog-ops/house-upgrade-stardew/lock/en/count-input.md
--- docs/blog-ops/house-upgrade-stardew/lock/en/body.md	2026-10-16 09:08:17
+++ docs/blog-ops/house-upgrade-stardew/lock/en/count-input.md	2026-10-16 09:08:17
@@ -44,7 +44,6 @@
 
 ![Three labeled stages: Upgrade 1 with Kitchen and Bedroom, Upgrade 2 with Empty room and Nursery, Upgrade 3 with Cellar and Same exterior, and a shared line reading 9×5 outdoors.](/blog/illustrations/house-upgrade-stardew/tier-rooms.en.webp)
 
-Schematic. Upgrade 1 is labeled Kitchen and Bedroom. Upgrade 2 is labeled Empty room and Nursery. Upgrade 3 is labeled Cellar and Same exterior. A shared line reads 9×5 outdoors.
 
 The third upgrade adds a cellar under the house. Enter it from the kitchen. The cellar starts with 33 casks. Those casks age cheese and wine, and also Goat Cheese, Beer, Mead, and Pale Ale, and that aging raises their quality and value. The cask recipe from this upgrade is 20 Wood and 1 Hardwood. You can set a cask somewhere else, but it accepts goods only while it is in the cellar. The outside of the house stays the same as the previous upgrade ([Farmhouse](https://stardewvalleywiki.com/Farmhouse), [Carpenter's Shop](https://stardewvalleywiki.com/Carpenter%27s_Shop), [Cask](https://stardewvalleywiki.com/Cask)).
 
@@ -62,7 +61,6 @@
 
 ![Two paths and two examples: Upgrade with 3 days; Renovation with After upgrade 2, Instant, and Refunds gold; Remove crib with Free; Dining room with 150,000g.](/blog/illustrations/house-upgrade-stardew/upgrade-or-renovation.en.webp)
 
-Schematic. The upgrade path reads Upgrade and 3 days. The renovation path reads Renovation, After upgrade 2, Instant, and Refunds gold. Remove crib reads Free. Dining room reads 150,000g.
 
 After the second farmhouse upgrade, Robin offers house renovations. You order one and it finishes immediately. To undo it, empty the new area first. Robin then returns the gold, and the refund arrives at once ([Carpenter's Shop](https://stardewvalleywiki.com/Carpenter%27s_Shop), [Farmhouse](https://stardewvalleywiki.com/Farmhouse)).
 
